\caption(Titles found by one Aho-Corasick pass over the 891 names, with survival rate and mean age. The figure shows the titles held by at least seven passengers)

Every passenger gets a title. Four titles cover 864 of the 891
passengers, and the remaining 27 hold the rare and aristocratic ones.
"Women and children first" shows up directly in the data:

- 16% of the 517 men (Mr) survived.
- 70% of the Misses and 79% of the Mrs survived.
- 57% of the 40 Masters survived. Their mean age is 4.6: Master was the
  title for boys.
- All six clergymen (Rev) died.

Mean ages are over passengers with a recorded age. The title is a strong
feature for imputing the 177 missing ages, which is why it appears in most
Titanic models.
\alttext(A bar chart of survival rate by title. Mr (517) is lowest at 0.16, Miss (182) is 0.70, Mrs (125) is highest at 0.79, Master (40) is 0.57, and Dr (7) is 0.43.)

> Cost against the size of the dictionary

To see the bound at work, take the first \(k\) distinct surnames on the
passenger list as the dictionary, for \(k\) from 1 to about 660, and
search the 24 917-byte stream of all names. The comparison is a KMP search
per surname (`algorithms::kmp_search`). For each \(k\) we record:

- the automaton's size and the number of matches \(z\);
- the transitions per character, \((\text{goto}+\text{failure})/n\),
  which the proof bounds by 2;
- the time for both methods, the fastest of three runs.

The timings depend on the machine; the step counts do not.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/aho_corasick_scaling.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

namespace alg = dm::algorithms;

template <class F> double fastest_ms(F&& f) {
  double best = 1e300;
  for (int rep = 0; rep < 3; ++rep) {
    const auto t0 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
    f();
    best = std::min(best, std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - t0).count());
  }
  return best;
}

int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto titanic = dm::datasets::titanic();
  std::string text;
  std::vector<std::string> surnames;
  std::set<std::string> seen;
  for (std::size_t r = 0; r < titanic.nrows(); ++r) {
    const auto& name = titanic.string_at("Name", r);
    text += name + "\n";
    const auto surname = name.substr(0, name.find(','));
    if (seen.insert(surname).second) surnames.push_back(surname);
  }
  std::print("Text: {} bytes; {} distinct surnames\n\n", text.size(), surnames.size());
  std::print("| k | pattern bytes m | states | matches z | transitions / char | failure / char | AC ms | KMP ms |\n");
  std::print("| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");

  std::vector<double> ks, ac_ms, kmp_ms, per_char;
  for (std::size_t k : {1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 400, 660}) {
    k = std::min(k, surnames.size());
    const std::vector<std::string> dict(surnames.begin(), surnames.begin() + k);
    std::size_t m = 0;
    for (const auto& s : dict) m += s.size();
    const alg::AhoCorasick ac(dict);
    const auto stats = ac.scan_stats(text);
    std::size_t kmp_matches = 0;
    const double t_ac = fastest_ms([&] { (void)ac.search(text); });
    const double t_kmp = fastest_ms([&] {
      kmp_matches = 0;
      for (const auto& s : dict) kmp_matches += alg::kmp_search(text, s).size();
    });
    const double steps = static_cast<double>(stats.goto_steps + stats.failure_steps) / stats.characters;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | {:.2f} | {:.2f} |\n", k, m, ac.state_count(), stats.matches,
               steps, static_cast<double>(stats.failure_steps) / stats.characters, t_ac, t_kmp);
    if (kmp_matches != stats.matches) std::print("MISMATCH: KMP found {}\n", kmp_matches);
    ks.push_back(std::log10(k));
    ac_ms.push_back(std::log10(t_ac));
    kmp_ms.push_back(std::log10(t_kmp));
    per_char.push_back(steps);
  }

  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                 .lines(ks, kmp_ms, "KMP per pattern", dm::RGB{220, 38, 38}, 2.0)
                 .points(ks, kmp_ms, "", dm::RGB{220, 38, 38}, 3.0)
                 .lines(ks, ac_ms, "Aho-Corasick", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 2.0)
                 .points(ks, ac_ms, "", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 3.0)
                 .title("Search time")
                 .x_label("log10 dictionary size k")
                 .y_label("log10 milliseconds"));
  layout.add(dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                 .lines(ks, per_char, "goto + failure", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 2.0)
                 .points(ks, per_char, "", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 3.0)
                 .lines({0.0, ks.back()}, {2.0, 2.0}, "bound 2", dm::RGB{17, 24, 39}, 1.0)
                 .y_limits(0, 2.2)
                 .title("Automaton transitions per character")
                 .x_label("log10 dictionary size k")
                 .y_label("transitions / character"));
  layout.size(1100, 440).save_svg("build/aho_corasick_scaling.svg");
}
```
